        """Date-only values mean midnight UTC. Datetimes must use `T`, seconds, and an
explicit `Z` or numeric timezone offset; natural-language dates, invalid
calendar dates, and timezone-less datetimes are rejected before `Date.parse()`
is used for normalization.

The service validates its own input and throws typed errors. The HTTP route only
parses JSON and maps those domain errors to `400`; future internal Project
callers cannot bypass the bound by skipping the route.
""",
        "strict timestamp explanation",
    )
    text = replace_once(
        text,
        "1. `exact_id` — case-insensitive exact stable-ID match;\n2. `exact_primary` — exact code, title, Recipe name/version, or filename match;\n3. `prefix_primary` — primary field begins with the complete normalized query;\n",
        "1. `exact_id` — byte-exact stable-ID match, then ASCII-case-insensitive fallback;\n2. `exact_primary` — byte-exact code/title/name/filename match, then ASCII-case-insensitive fallback;\n3. `prefix_primary` — the primary field begins with the raw or ASCII-folded complete query;\n",
        "ranking Unicode policy",
    )
    text = replace_once(
